Summary

Are you detail-oriented, technically minded and do you enjoy working with your hands? Would you like to join one of Europe’s leading manufacturers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position with our client in Waalwijk could be the perfect opportunity for you.

Job Description

As a Production Worker, you will contribute to the manufacturing of high-quality, tailor-made sandwich panels. These panels are used in various industries, including bodywork construction and defense. Depending on your experience, interests and the needs of the department, you will be assigned to different tasks within the production process.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, as part of a close-knit and supportive team. Using technical drawings and parts lists, you will transform individual raw materials into a finished product of excellent quality. Thanks to the variety of panels and tasks, no two working days are the same.

Accuracy, quality and teamwork are key within this role. The impact of your work is directly visible in the final product.

Responsibilities

Depending on the department, your tasks may include:

- Emptying, cleaning and preparing press tables;
- Collecting and preparing various raw materials;
- Producing and bonding sandwich panels;
- Cutting, deburring and sealing aluminum panels;
- Sawing, calibrating and adjusting materials such as foam, wood and composite to the correct thickness;
- Numbering, sorting and preparing parts for shipment;
- Operating machinery and, if qualified, an overhead crane;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

What We Ask

- You work accurately and have technical insight;
- You can read technical drawings and parts lists, or are willing to learn;
- You are a true team player;
- You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.

Are you looking for a warehouse job in an international team with clear working hours and opportunities to grow? Start as a Warehouse Employee at GXO Logistics in Tilburg. You earn €14.99 gross per hour and receive travel allowance and pension.

You work with clothing and accessories. Depending on your department, you collect, pack, check or move products.

Your tasks can include:

- Picking orders with a scanner;
- Packing and checking products;
- Processing returned items;
- Receiving and storing products;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Keeping your workplace clean and safe.

You will receive training for the tasks in your department. There are also opportunities to learn different warehouse processes.

You work either a fixed morning shift or in two shifts:

- Morning shift: 06:00 to 14:45;
- Afternoon shift: 15:15 to 00:00.

You like active work and enjoy working together with others.

We ask:

- You speak English at B1 level or higher;
- You are physically fit and can stand and walk for longer periods;
- You are available for a fixed morning shift or two-shift schedule;
- You have your own accommodation and transport;
- You can apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are available full-time.

Experience in a warehouse is useful, but not listed as a requirement for this job.
